+ *   iceusb=1        bring-up and console. Needs the tablet: on any CPU that is not Qualcomm's (MIDR implementer 0x51,
+ *                   the tablet reads 0x512f0021) nothing is mapped or touched; a bring-up that stops removes the tap
+ *   iceusb=2        read only: the power, clock and controller census lines; nothing is written
+ *   iceusb_smmu=1   with 1 or 2: also read stream 0x40's SMMU route from global page 0 (ID0, SMR, S2CR) and its context
+ *                   bank's own page (SCTLR, TCR, TTBR0). Never Global Register Space 1: it aborts from EL1 on SM8850
+ *   iceusb_steps=M  bring-up parts, default 7: 1 the controller's block reset (GCC_USB30_PRIM_BCR), 2 the M31 eUSB2
+ *                   PHY's reset and init, 4 power-up writes (GDSC, branch clocks, TCSR reference) where they read off
+ *   iceusb_trace=N  the first N controller events after each bus reset go to the log (default 24)
+ * Without iceusb= (0): hakios_iceland_usbcon_init() returns at its first test; nothing is mapped, allocated or hooked,
+ * and the loader log's tap stays NULL.
+ *
+ * Why a start from scratch, not U-Boot's gadget (iceland-u-boot, build tree 8489df99, read for facts):
+ *   `fastboot continue` ends cmd/fastboot.c's loop in udc_device_put() (:131-132), a device_remove() of the DWC3
+ *   peripheral: dwc3_remove() (drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c:1248-1256) ends the gadget, zeroes the event buffer registers
+ *   and clears RUN_STOP; dwc3_shutdown_phy() runs the M31 PHY's power_off, which asserts GCC_QUSB2PHY_PRIM_BCR
+ *   (drivers/phy/qcom/phy-qcom-m31-eusb2.c:188-196); then device_remove() switches the power domain off
+ *   (drivers/core/device-remove.c:262-266): qcom_power_set() sets SW_COLLAPSE in GCC_USB30_PRIM_GDSCR
