+ *   kaanapali GCC and TCSR clock drivers have no disable: drivers/clk/qcom/clock-kaanapali.c:240, 295-297), the RPMh
+ *   rails and the eUSB2 repeater stay as U-Boot set them (no regulator disable, no repeater exit). So at the
+ *   hand-off nothing of U-Boot's gadget survives (its DMA memory is U-Boot's, its controller state lost with the GDSC):
+ *   this driver powers the block up again, resets it, initialises the PHY and the core, and enumerates afresh. The
+ *   census line says what it actually found.
+ *
+ * DMA and the SMMU, with no SMMU write: U-Boot's device tree gives usb@a600000 no iommus (arch/arm/dts/
+ * kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts:193-215), so its qcom-hyp-smmu never connects the stream: stream 0x40 is routed as ABL's
+ * fastboot left it, and U-Boot's own fastboot DMA works through it from its heap below relocaddr 0xaffda4000 (tablet,
+ * runs/a3/probe), above 4 GiB. data-a-live measured the same SoC after `fastboot boot` (wsl/qcomusb/soc/Sm8850.h:14-16,
+ * 50-53): stream 0x40 -> bank 3, translation off, stage 2 bypass, so DMA at physical addresses. The buffers here are the
+ * kernel's own pages, physically contiguous, below 4 GiB when the kernel has such pages (else anywhere), used through
+ * the kernel's cacheable view with clean+invalidate to the point of coherency around every hand-over: right whether the
+ * bypass route is coherent or not (U-Boot and data-a-live do the same).
+ *
+ * Never touched: storage, the SMMU (written), the eUSB2 repeater, the QMP USB3/DP PHY, Type-C, the charger, interrupts
+ * (the controller is polled, its event interrupt masked).
+ *
+ * Sources and licences.
+ *   The structure follows UniXNU-piano package/PianoDwc3 (Copyright (c) 2026, UniXNU-piano contributors,
+ *   BSD-2-Clause-Patent; read at ea12db1): the takeover order (PianoDwc3.cpp:1586-1702), the polled gadget core
