+#if defined(XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX) && XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX
+/*
+ * q35/q35b, deviation D25: a diagnostic of our own, after lenzhang's stderr-log idea (xp8/main
+ * docs/boot-time.md; no source available) and with no UniXNU equivalent.
+ *
+ *   stderr-log=1  every write(2) to fd 1 or 2 of any process is copied (up to 512 bytes of the user's
+ *                 buffer) into the kernel log as     stderr[pid comm fdN]: <the bytes>
+ *   stderr-log=2  the same, plus every write(2) of pid 1 (launchd/init) on *any* fd, as
+ *                                                    pid1w[fdN <path>]: <the bytes>
+ *                 where <path> is vn_getpath() of the file's vnode ("non-vnode type N" for sockets and
+ *                 pipes), resolved on each line so a reused fd cannot report a stale one.
+ *
+ * so the text a process writes to its stderr (or, for init, to its own log fd) at a stop is not lost with
+ * the console. It never changes the syscall's result or behaviour: a failed copyin prints nothing and the
+ * write goes on; the hook runs only when the argument is set. The general budget is 64 lines a second; at
+ * level 2 pid 1 has its own budget of 256 a second, and after 100 s of uptime it is exempt altogether, so
+ * the last lines before an abort cannot be dropped. Drops are counted and said so at the next second.
+ * Off by default; the variable is a boot-arg tunable.
+ *
+ * w5-bt: likewise iceland-bt-scan (the Bluetooth scan check, /private/var/ngpu/bin/iceland-bt-scan) always, and
+ * bluetoothd when the boot-arg icebt_log=1 is set (its power state line "Update Dynamic Store with state On").
+ *
+ * w4-audio round 7: with stderr-log off, the fd 1 and fd 2 writes of the recorder alone (a p_comm that begins
+ * "iceland-audio-r": /private/var/ngpu/bin/iceland-audio-rec, truncated to "iceland-audio-re") are logged too, through
+ * the same general window and the same format. The tablet's line has stderr-log=0, and the recorder's start, STOPPED,
+ * DONE and FAIL lines say what a recording did; without this they reach no log at all (its stdout is the tablet's).
+ * w5-camera: the camera's userland is named the same way, for the same reason: the probe and the test job's tools
+ * ("iceland-camera-probe", "iceland-camera-..."), the host app ("IcelandCameraHost") and the extension ("IcelandCamera"),
+ * whose "CMIO ..." lines say what activation, the provider and the stream did.
+ *
+ * The hook lives in writev_internal only: write_internal() builds its uio and calls it, and every other
+ * write path (write_nocancel, pwrite, writev, pwritev and their _nocancel forms) funnels through it too,
+ * so one write is logged once. (q35 hooked both, and so printed every write twice.)
+ */
