+/*
+ * AGXAccelerator: macOS 27's Metal accelerator for the Pad's Adreno 840 (S11 g6a; plan D21: our A840 hardware half under
+ * UniXNU's OS contract). macOS only (XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX); the iPadOS path keeps RedwoodGPU's IOAcceleratorES naming.
+ *
+ * What macOS asks for (read in UniXNU and in lenzhang's piano, read only; no code of theirs is copied):
+ *   - Metal makes a device only for a registry IOAccelerator: IOGPU's +[IOGPUMetalDevice registerAcceleratorService:] loads
+ *     <MetalPluginName>.bundle from /Library/GPUBundles; with none, WindowServer waits 30 s and aborts (piano 11-10
+ *     package/NativeSoftGpu/NativeSoftGpu.cpp:5-10; piano 613a209 docs/drivers/soft-metal.md:19).
+ *   - The C++ class is named AGXAccelerator and derives from IOGraphicsFamily's IOAccelerator, a 136-byte class with no
+ *     operational overrides (UniXNU 9248bdac scripts/data/ioaccelerator-base-abi-26C5035r.json:2-21, read from this
+ *     kernelcache, d1003b51...; AdrenoMetal c1351337 OriginalAcceleratorABI.h:8-14). Turnip matches that name
+ *     (TU_DARWIN_SERVICE=AGXAccelerator) and macOS's sandbox profiles admit it (Adreno740 a8fa18f
+ *     NativeAdrenoAccelerator.cpp:7-8; piano 613a209 docs/drivers/gpu-userspace.md:158-159).
+ *   - Its personality carries MetalPluginName NativeAdrenoMetal and MetalPluginClassName NativeAdrenoMetalDevice in match
+ *     category IOAccelerator, and matches the nub the GPU stack publishes once the GPU is up, NativeAdrenoGpuPublished:
+ *     before that WindowServer must find no accelerator (piano 613a209 docs/drivers/gpu.md:43-45, gpu-userspace.md:160-163).
+ *   - The render server is WindowServer, where iPadOS has backboardd (Adreno740 7487f72 NativeAdrenoPublish.cpp:28-35).
+ *
+ * How the class gets IOAccelerator as its superclass without a link to IOGraphicsFamily: it is C++-derived from IOService
+ * (the same 136 bytes; every virtual is IOService's, as IOAccelerator overrides none: the JSON above,
+ * "operational_overrides": []), and its OSMetaClass is made at run time, once IOGraphicsFamily is loaded, with
+ * IOAccelerator's metaclass (found by name) as its superclass, between OSMetaClass::preModLoad and postModLoad for the
+ * kernel. UniXNU registers its late classes the same way (Adreno740 a8fa18f NativeAdrenoAccelerator.cpp:5-8, UniXNU
+ * 9248bdac scripts/build-adreno740-accelerator.py:2-5), and binds the base's constructor, destructor and metaclass by
+ * address (ibid. :92-94); this one finds the metaclass by name and needs neither of the others: they are IOService's.
+ * IOKit's class matching, OSDynamicCast and IOObjectConformsTo all walk the metaclass chain, so to every one of them the
+ * object is an IOAccelerator. The base is checked first (IOService's direct subclass, IOService's size), or nothing is
+ * registered. The late registration needs libkern's lock order (OSKext.cpp, OSKextLockForModLoad).
+ *
+ * Boot-arg iceagx=1: publish the accelerator at boot without a GPU behind it (the QEMU / desk proof of the IOKit side): the
+ * class, the nub, the matched personality, the registry entry that IOServiceMatching("IOAccelerator") finds. Every open is
+ * named in the log, and refused unless iceagx_client=1 (below). Without it nothing here runs, unless the GPU's
+ * persistent service names the plug-in (icegpu=6 icegpu_persist=1 icegpu_metal=1: RedwoodGPUNameMetalPlugin publishes, and
+ * withdraws on the way down). Lines start with "agx: ".
+ * Boot-arg iceagx_client=1: open type 0x4147 gets AGXDeviceUserClient, the NativeAdreno ABI v2 user client (g6b-1). While the
+ * GPU serves (icegpu=6: the stage-6 API of hakios_iceland_gpu.c is up) a connection gets its own GPU space and every method:
+ * buffers (BoAlloc, BoImport, BoMap, BoFree, CPU views), submissions and fences, queues, the device facts, metadata. With no
+ * GPU it stays g6b-0's skeleton: the selector probe and Query answered, every other method refused (below).
+ * Boot-arg iceagx_selftest=1 (with iceagx_client=1): a kernel client drives the skeleton's wire once after the publish.
+ * iceagx_selftest=2: a kernel client drives every method (on the A840 when the GPU is up: the tablet probe's window,
