+# iceland w3-power (display sleep, boot-arg disp-sleep): two entries of the same collection that the fixture does not name.
+# Each is identified by its slot's diversity, which is the pointer-authentication discriminator of the original method's name:
+#   slot 419 = IOMobileFramebufferLegacy::do_power_state_change_gated(), which the family calls at every change of its two power
+#     states (its own entry returns 0); the backend overrides it, so the slot gets a prototype;
+#   slot 322 = IOMobileFramebuffer::powerstate_notify(bool, bool), the power state notification to the display's clients: its
+#     original entry is bound as a C entry (the backend does not override it).
