+//
+// iceland audio stage 1: the Pad 4's speakers as the built-in output device macOS's audio server takes, an IOAudio2Device
+// with the UID "Speaker", on a null transport. Boot-arg icesnddev=1; without it nothing here runs.
+//
+// Provenance: lenzhang/UniXNU-xiaomipad8pro main dcfbe72, package/PianoAudio/PianoAudioDevice.cpp (sha256 d2eff0ec...,
+// BSD-2-Clause-Patent; the copyright line and licence above are package/PianoAudio/LICENSE's, sha256 4631e4bc...), the
+// IOAudio2Device top half of piano's audio driver, itself after UniXNU-droidvm e29d087 package/DroidVMAudio.cpp
+// (BSD-2-Clause-Patent; piano's package/PianoAudio/UPSTREAM). Taken over: the
+// device and user-client classes, the registry description, the engine and the run-time link under the family's classes.
+// Changed for iceland: one device (the speaker; no microphone yet), the names, the boot argument and its worker, the
+// log lines, the user client's locking properties, and the transport: each period goes to redwood_audio_play()
+// (bsd/dev/redwood_audio.c), /dev/redwood-audio's own path -- no sink on the tablet today (silence: nothing reaches the
+// hardware), QEMU's virtio sound device with virtio_sound=1, later the DSP's sound service (hakios_iceland_adsp.c).
+//
+// How the audio server sees it (piano's notes, kept): its IOAudio2 manager matches IOServiceMatching("IOAudio2Device") and
+// tests IOObjectConformsTo, then opens an IOAudio2DeviceUserClient. The family kext is in the collection (IOAVFamily needs
+// it), so its two class names are taken and its subclass contract is closed: these classes have their own names, implement
+// the whole user-client interface themselves, and at attach their metaclasses are linked under the family's, which is what
+// matching and IOObjectConformsTo test. No family code runs on these objects.
+//   registry   the description as dictionary keys with spaces ("device UID", "output streams", ...); sample rates are
+//              32.32 fixed-point 64-bit numbers
+//   open       IOServiceOpen type 0; a notification port of type 0
+//   memory     type 0: the engine status (at least 0x28 bytes: +0 zero sample time, +8 its host time, +0x10 seed, +0x20 the
+//              server's write end); type 0x10000000 + stream id: the stream's ring
+//   selectors  0 StartIO, 1 StopIO, 2 SetControlValue, 3 PerformConfigChange, 4 SetNominalSampleRate, 5
+//              SetStreamCurrentFormat, 6 SetStreamActive, 10 / 11 start / stop with flags, 12 SetClientDescription; the
+//              server also writes "exclusive access owner" (hog mode) through setProperties
+//   I/O        no trap: the server writes the ring at the zero time stamp's position; the engine takes one period at a time
+// Lines start with "icesnddev: ".
+//
+// w4-audio (audio stage 2 / 3): icesnddev=2 publishes a second device beside the speaker, the microphone: UID "Mic", one
+// input stream (48 kHz, 1 x 16 bit, terminal 'micr'), piano's second device. Its engine fills the period the position just
+// passed from redwood_audio_capture() (bsd/dev/redwood_audio.c: the source a driver registered -- on the tablet the DSP's
+// capture service, hakios_iceland_adsp.c icemic_svc=1 -- or silence). Volume and mute stay the audio server's: its
+// VirtualAudio layer makes the "Speaker" UID a speaker port with its own software volume, so what reaches the ring is
+// already at the user's level, and the kernel's cap (icesnd_cap) bounds it below that; a SetControlValue call is logged.
+// icesnddev_beep=T: at T s of uptime, if the audio server holds the speaker, six presses 3 s apart, the letter q and
+// Command-J in turn, through the HID keyboard (iceland_hid_line): with the Finder in front and nothing to select the
+// letter is the alert sound -- a sound from macOS with nobody at the tablet. Off by default.
