+/*
+ * hakios/HAS_STD_PAC: mirror libkern/os/base.h's data-pointer decision here so the assembler sees
+ * it too.  machine_routines_asm.h includes this header but NOT base.h, and the data-pointer auth
+ * macros (AUTDA_DIVERSIFIED etc.) must be gated on the exact same condition the C field qualifiers
+ * (XNU_PTRAUTH_SIGNED_PTR) are, or asm will autda a field the C side stored plain -> FPAC.  The
+ * macOS target defines XNU_PTRAUTH_SIGNED_DATA_PTRS (base/xnu-build.sh): there data pointers are
+ * signed, the loader makes the keys per boot and the kernel signs its own MH_FILESET collection.
+ * A build without that define (the iOS target) leaves them plain; code pointers / return addresses
+ * and the pacga state hash are authenticated in either case.
